{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\np=json.load(open('../direct-checks/e03642c1801746c7b24a03fc1dc1d643/plan.json'));p['harness'].pop('source',None);print(json.dumps(p))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"{\"description\": \"For C-read-context, run a generated three-Peer election/replication prefix. First confirm one forwarded request as a control. Then admit node 2 context A and node 3 context B while delaying A heartbeats, deliver a generated B heartbeat to node 2 and its reply to leader, and observe all emitted remote replies plus destination ReadyToRead. Distinct destinations identify the two operations independently of their contexts. The fixed stopping point is completion of that response handler and the resulting reply deliveries.\", \"claim_id\": \"C-read-context\", \"binding_ids\": [\"BD-read-emit\", \"BD-read-receive\"], \"harness\": {\"execution_package\": \"./internal/raft\", \"files\": {}, \"kind\": \"go_test\", \"description\": \"TestAssuranceForwardedReadContexts uses Peer.Launch/Tick/ReadIndex/Handle/GetUpdate/Commit with existing TestLogDB and synchronous update processing.\", \"semantic_changes\": [\"Replace transport with a deterministic queue delivering actual generated messages.\", \"Use existing volatile TestLogDB instead of production disk backend, with no crash/restart.\", \"Synchronously consume committed bootstrap and noop entries; no application query or NodeHost endpoint is measured.\", \"Read private state only to verify setup/admission and report pending-count diagnostics.\"], \"prerequisites\": [{\"alias\": \"admit\", \"event\": \"admitted\", \"conditions\": [{\"field\": \"admitted\", \"op\": \"eq\", \"value\": true, \"reference\": null}]}], \"legality\": {\"source_ids\": [\"S-launch\", \"S-peer-bootstrap\", \"S-peer-cycle\", \"S-test-storage\", \"S-test-storage-append\", \"S-engine-order\", \"S-message-dispatch\", \"S-read-batch\", \"S-heartbeat-producer\", \"S-replication\", \"S-start\"], \"expectation_ids\": [\"S-update-contract\", \"S-read-identity-contract\"], \"binding_ids\": [\"BD-read-emit\", \"BD-read-receive\"], \"derivation\": \"Launch creates three regular members with distinct addresses and in-memory TestLogDB. Driver drains bootstrap committed config entries, applies each through Peer.ApplyConfigChange, advances applied index, and uses Tick only on node 1 until the generated vote exchange elects it. All later messages come from GetUpdate. Before sending any message, Append and SetState save update contents; committed entries are synchronously applied, Commit acknowledges the update, and NotifyRaftLastApplied reports application. This is a stronger persistence order than the implementation requires and does not serialize distinct read operations. No protocol state or pending record is injected; private fields are read solely for prerequisite/diagnostic observations. Later-context heartbeat and reply are generated by the target. Delaying earlier heartbeats is permitted asynchronous scheduling. TestLogDB substitutes storage in a no-crash history; no filesystem or goroutine shutdown lifecycle belongs to Peer/TestLogDB. The driver does not use the newTestRaft helper that overrides configuration barriers.\", \"applicability\": \"No crashes, loss of storage, snapshots, membership transitions or Byzantine messages; network scheduling permits finite delays and invokes Peer APIs serially.\", \"unresolved\": [], \"conflicts\": [], \"alternatives\": [\"The source producer excludes contextual observer responses, so none are invented.\", \"All original messages remain captured; the schedule ends at the first later-context quorum response, not upon oracle success or failure.\"]}}, \"monitors\": [{\"id\": \"M-read-context\", \"checker_id\": \"K-read-context\", \"event\": \"response\", \"binding_ids\": [\"BD-read-emit\", \"BD-read-receive\"], \"grounding\": {\"source_ids\": [\"S-read-response\", \"S-read-aggregation\", \"S-forward-read\", \"S-peer-cycle\"], \"expectation_ids\": [\"S-read-identity-contract\"], \"binding_ids\": [\"BD-read-emit\", \"BD-read-receive\"], \"derivation\": \"C-read-context is evaluated on emitted ReadIndexResp after actual confirmation. Original contexts are recorded at actual pending admission. The pair (scenario, requester) is unique independently of the compared context because each requester has one request in each scenario. Destination selects the original request; a replacement context therefore remains observable rather than failing an equality filter.\", \"applicability\": \"Single stable term and membership with current-term commitment; single-request control and overlapping two-request prefix.\", \"unresolved\": [], \"conflicts\": [], \"alternatives\": []}, \"applicability_conditions\": [], \"admission_alias\": \"admit\"}], \"observable_properties\": [{\"checker_id\": \"K-read-context\", \"kind\": \"event_assertion\", \"trigger\": {\"field\": \"observed\", \"op\": \"eq\", \"value\": true, \"reference\": null}, \"assertion\": {\"field\": \"context\", \"op\": \"eq\", \"value\": null, \"reference\": \"admit.expected_context\"}, \"antecedent\": null, \"identity_fields\": [\"scenario\", \"requester\"], \"description\": \"Each emitted response must preserve the admitted operation context for its independently identified requester and scenario.\"}], \"uncertainties\": [\"Peer-level identity check does not measure NodeHost request timeout, application lookup, or whole-cluster linearizability.\", \"Undelivered earlier heartbeat traffic remains explicitly delayed; no lost automatic-continuation claim is inferred.\"]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"The trusted run observed the mismatch: node 2’s request was admitted with context `201/2001`, but its response and resulting `ReadyToRead` carried node 3’s context, `202/2002`. The single-request control preserved its context. This supports the scoped response-correlation defect; it does not establish a stale read or an infinite stall.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > submission-review.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \\\"action\\\": \\\"review\\\",\n  \\\"artifact_id\\\": \\\"37c39f3b408c4fe38239b3a3597d61f3\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Review the fixed version 1 check and actual clean-copy observations against C-read-context version 1, including generated history, substitutions, independent identity and scoped consequences.\\\",\n  \\\"review_items\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"aspect\\\": \\\"checker_correspondence\\\",\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"no_issue_found\\\",\n      \\\"source_ids\\\": [\\\"S-read-identity-contract\\\", \\\"S-read-contract\\\", \\\"S-read-aggregation\\\", \\\"S-read-response\\\", \\\"S-forward-read\\\", \\\"S-read-consumer\\\", \\\"S-launch\\\", \\\"S-peer-bootstrap\\\", \\\"S-peer-cycle\\\", \\\"S-test-storage\\\", \\\"S-test-storage-append\\\", \\\"S-update-contract\\\", \\\"S-message-dispatch\\\", \\\"S-read-batch\\\", \\\"S-heartbeat-producer\\\", \\\"S-core-commit\\\", \\\"S-log-guards\\\"],\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Reviewed the fixed plan and internal/raft/assurance_generated_test.go at direct-checks/e03642c1801746c7b24a03fc1dc1d643 and execution 88621c84c65e4fc48ac49425d0866bff stdout/stderr, rather than relying on process PASS or matching checker IDs. Requirement applicability: SystemCtx explicitly identifies a ReadIndex operation; ReadyToRead denotes readiness for a prior batch; the consumer selects that exact context. The obligation applies when the leader releases an admitted remote record, not to every pending request or a success deadline. Legal prefix: Launch constructs three fresh regular Peers and bootstrap entries. The driver stores entries/state before exposing messages, applies only actual committed configuration/noop entries, acknowledges updates and reports applied indexes. It ticks node 1, routes generated vote and replication messages, and checks all members know leader 1, have applied commitment beyond bootstrap, and the leader has current-term commitment. Output records term 2 and commit 4. TestLogDB is a no-crash storage substitute; transport is a serial deterministic queue. No role, log, remote match, pending read, or acknowledgement is fabricated. The chosen finite schedule delays earlier contextual heartbeat messages and delivers the later actual heartbeat and generated reply; it does not require simultaneous handler execution. Producer continuity: Peer.ReadIndex on nodes 2 and 3 produces actual forwarded requests; admissions inspect the live leader pending records, requiring stored requester/context to match issued values. The one-response quorum includes leader 1 and actual voter 2 in a three-voter configuration. Source confirm then releases the prefix; the observed suffix has zero pending records and two replies. Independent correlation: (scenario, requester) uniquely selects one admission for each output; requester is read from response To, not the compared context, and no expected-context equality filters outputs. CA_EVENT results are copied from actual exported message fields; destination ReadyToRead is independently read from Peer.GetUpdate after Handle. The monitor has no applicability exclusion and compares the full Low/High context string against admit.expected_context. Actual observations: single requester 2 retains 101/1001 at index 4. In overlap, requester 2 was admitted with 201/2001 but received 202/2002; requester 3 was admitted with and received 202/2002. Both destination ReadyToRead observations carry 202/2002. The monitor correlated all three results, reports no parser errors or missing results, and marks the requester-2 overlap comparison violated. This answers the original remote-prefix identity question in a generated stable-term history. Source attribution agrees: confirm returns stored records, but the remote emission branch uses triggering m.Hint/m.HintHigh rather than each s.ctx. The local branch and single-outstanding-request path are protective alternatives; the successful control is retained and does not contradict the scoped overlapping-prefix defect. Finite undelivered traffic is explicit and the stopping point is independent of equality. No claim of lost automatic continuation, client timeout, stale application data or global consensus failure follows from this measurement.\\\",\n      \\\"counterevidence\\\": [],\n      \\\"limitations\\\": [\n        \\\"The measured boundary is Peer ReadIndexResp identity, with destination ReadyToRead as an additional observation; NodeHost RequestState completion and application lookup are not executed.\\\",\n        \\\"TestLogDB and deterministic transport replace production persistence and networking in a no-crash, stable-membership history; disk and transport implementation defects are outside this check.\\\",\n        \\\"Earlier heartbeat messages remain delayed. The finite suffix is not a closed-state recurrence or an infinite-stall proof.\\\",\n        \\\"Different operations at different destinations provide unique independent correlation; multiple overlapping requests at the same destination are not measured.\\\",\n        \\\"No stale-read safety consequence is observed; a likely unmatched pending batch follows from source consumption but is not an executed client endpoint.\\\"\n      ],\n      \\\"report_title\\\": \\\"合并读确认时，较早远端请求的上下文被替换\\\",\n      \\\"report_answer\\\": \\\"三节点同一任期内，较晚请求的心跳确认释放两个远端读请求；节点 2 原上下文为 201/2001，实际响应及 ReadyToRead 均携带节点 3 的 202/2002。单请求对照保持原上下文；此结果仅证明响应关联错误，不证明陈旧读取或无限停滞。\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"feedback\\\": {\n    \\\"ref_ids\\\": [\\\"df58639a581544c288c0192bc5c095e4\\\", \\\"B-read-confirm\\\", \\\"B-read-receive\\\", \\\"37c39f3b408c4fe38239b3a3597d61f3\\\", \\\"88621c84c65e4fc48ac49425d0866bff\\\", \\\"S-read-response\\\", \\\"S-read-aggregation\\\"],\n    \\\"answered\\\": \\\"A generated three-Peer history reaches overlapping forwarded requests and prefix release. The earlier remote requester receives the later request context, and its Peer exports that substituted context in ReadyToRead. The single-request control retains its identity. The fixed monitor reports a complete violated comparison for C-read-context; this review finds no current correspondence issue within that scope.\\\",\n    \\\"remaining\\\": [\\\"NodeHost completion/timeout and application-level consequences remain unmeasured; they are independent of the completed Peer identity comparison.\\\", \\\"Other authority, membership, persistence and recovery relationships remain available for independent investigation.\\\"],\n    \\\"understanding\\\": \\\"updated\\\",\n    \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Retain actual contrary control behavior and distinguish the observed correlation error from broader progress or safety hypotheses. Incorporate the conditional source relationship at the next relevant map handoff.\\\"\n  }\n}\nEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-04_11-52-07-dragonboat_raft-real-run --submission submission-review.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
